FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/interpreter.rs:1765 — The `profile_enter` function has a branch `if self.call_depth != 0 { return false; }` that excludes user function bodies from line profiling, attributing their time to the call-site line instead. This branch has no test coverage: no test calls a user function within a profiled block to verify the call-site attribution behavior described in the doc comment.
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:1957 — The `execute_line` function overwrites `last_profile` on each multiline block run (`self.last_profile = Some(...)`), but there is no test verifying that `.profile` shows only the last block's timings rather than accumulating or retaining the first block.
3. [MINOR] src/repl/weight.rs:224 — The test `val_bytes_covers_text_lists_records_and_sharing` only exercises `Value::Nothing`, `Value::Text`, `Value::List`, and `Value::Record`. Missing coverage for `Value::Number`, `Value::YesNo`, `Value::Builtin`, `Value::Object`, and `Value::Function` variants.
4. [STYLE] src/repl/weight.rs:82-87 — `human_bytes` labels 1024-based units as "KB"/"MB" (e.g., `10.0 KB (10240 B)`). The standard for 1024-based units is "KiB"/"MiB"; "KB"/"MB" conventionally mean 1000/1,000,000.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
